## 4. Key Concepts & Building Blocks

### 4.1 DNS (Domain Name System)

```
Client → DNS Resolver → Root Server → TLD Server → Authoritative Server
                                                         ↓
                                                   IP Address returned
```

- Translates domain names to IP addresses
- Hierarchical, distributed database
- Uses UDP port 53
- TTL (Time-to-Live) controls caching duration
- Types: A (IPv4), AAAA (IPv6), CNAME (alias), MX (mail), NS (nameserver)

### 4.2 IP Addressing & Networking Basics

- **TCP**: Reliable, ordered, connection-oriented (HTTP, FTP, SMTP)
- **UDP**: Unreliable, unordered, connectionless (DNS, video streaming, gaming)
- **HTTP/HTTPS**: Application layer protocol over TCP
- **WebSocket**: Full-duplex communication over single TCP connection
- **gRPC**: High-performance RPC framework using HTTP/2 and Protocol Buffers

### 4.3 Throughput vs Latency vs Bandwidth

| Term | Definition | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **Latency** | Time for a single request to complete | 50ms response time |
| **Throughput** | Number of requests processed per unit time | 10,000 req/sec |
| **Bandwidth** | Maximum data transfer capacity | 1 Gbps network link |

### 4.4 Availability & Reliability

**Availability** = Uptime / (Uptime + Downtime) × 100%

| Availability | Downtime/Year | Downtime/Month | Downtime/Week |
|-------------|---------------|-----------------|----------------|
| 99% (two 9s) | 3.65 days | 7.31 hours | 1.68 hours |
| 99.9% (three 9s) | 8.77 hours | 43.83 min | 10.08 min |
| 99.99% (four 9s) | 52.60 min | 4.38 min | 1.01 min |
| 99.999% (five 9s) | 5.26 min | 26.30 sec | 6.05 sec |

**Reliability** = Probability the system performs correctly over a period of time

**MTBF** = Mean Time Between Failures  
**MTTR** = Mean Time To Recovery  
**Availability** = MTBF / (MTBF + MTTR)

### 4.5 Redundancy & Replication

- **Active-Active**: All replicas serve traffic simultaneously
- **Active-Passive**: Standby takes over on primary failure
- **Hot Standby**: Standby is always running, ready to take over
- **Cold Standby**: Standby is provisioned but not running

