## 12. Message Queues & Event-Driven Architecture

### 12.1 Why Message Queues?

- **Decoupling**: Producer and consumer don't need to know about each other
- **Async processing**: Producer doesn't wait for consumer
- **Load leveling**: Buffer spikes in traffic
- **Reliability**: Messages survive consumer failures
- **Scalability**: Scale producers and consumers independently

### 12.2 Message Queue Patterns

#### Point-to-Point (Queue)
```
[Producer] → [Queue] → [Consumer]
                     (one consumer gets each message)
```

#### Publish-Subscribe (Topic)
```
[Publisher] → [Topic] → [Subscriber 1]
                     → [Subscriber 2]
                     → [Subscriber 3]
              (all subscribers get the message)
```

#### Request-Reply
```
[Requester] → [Request Queue] → [Responder]
[Requester] ← [Reply Queue]   ← [Responder]
```

### 12.3 Delivery Guarantees

| Guarantee | Description | Trade-off |
|-----------|------------|-----------|
| **At-most-once** | Message delivered 0 or 1 time | May lose messages |
| **At-least-once** | Message delivered 1 or more times | May duplicate messages |
| **Exactly-once** | Message delivered exactly once | Most complex, highest overhead |

### 12.4 Message Queue Comparison

| Feature | Kafka | RabbitMQ | Amazon SQS | Amazon SNS |
|---------|-------|----------|------------|------------|
| **Type** | Distributed log | Message broker | Managed queue | Pub/Sub |
| **Ordering** | Per partition | Per queue (FIFO) | FIFO (optional) | No ordering |
| **Throughput** | Very high (millions/sec) | Moderate (10K-50K/sec) | High (managed) | High (managed) |
| **Retention** | Configurable (days/forever) | Until consumed | 14 days max | No retention |
| **Consumer model** | Pull (poll) | Push | Pull (poll) | Push |
| **Replay** | Yes (offset-based) | No (once consumed) | No | No |
| **Best for** | Event streaming, logs, analytics | Task queues, RPC | Simple queuing | Fan-out notifications |

### 12.5 Event-Driven Architecture

```
[Order Service] ──OrderPlaced──→ [Event Bus/Kafka]
                                       │
                     ┌─────────────────┼──────────────────┐
                     ↓                 ↓                  ↓
             [Payment Service]  [Inventory Service]  [Notification Service]
```

**Event Sourcing:**
- Store all changes as a sequence of events
- Current state = replay of all events
- Audit trail for free
- Can rebuild state at any point in time

**CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation):**
```
[Write Model] ──events──→ [Event Store] ──→ [Read Model]
     ↑                                          ↓
  Commands                                   Queries
(Create, Update, Delete)               (Read, Search, Report)
```

