## 14. API Design

### 14.1 REST API Best Practices

```
GET    /api/v1/users          → List users
GET    /api/v1/users/{id}     → Get user by ID
POST   /api/v1/users          → Create user
PUT    /api/v1/users/{id}     → Update entire user
PATCH  /api/v1/users/{id}     → Partial update
DELETE /api/v1/users/{id}     → Delete user

GET    /api/v1/users/{id}/orders     → Get orders for a user
POST   /api/v1/users/{id}/orders     → Create order for a user
```

**Best Practices:**
- Use nouns, not verbs (✓ /users, ✗ /getUsers)
- Use plural nouns (✓ /users, ✗ /user)
- Version your API (/api/v1/, /api/v2/)
- Use proper HTTP status codes
- Support pagination, filtering, sorting
- Use HATEOAS for discoverability

### 14.2 HTTP Status Codes

| Code | Meaning | Use Case |
|------|---------|----------|
| 200 | OK | Successful GET/PUT/PATCH |
| 201 | Created | Successful POST |
| 204 | No Content | Successful DELETE |
| 301 | Moved Permanently | URL redirect |
| 304 | Not Modified | Cached response valid |
| 400 | Bad Request | Validation error |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Not authenticated |
| 403 | Forbidden | Not authorized |
| 404 | Not Found | Resource doesn't exist |
| 409 | Conflict | Duplicate or conflicting state |
| 429 | Too Many Requests | Rate limited |
| 500 | Internal Server Error | Server bug |
| 502 | Bad Gateway | Upstream failure |
| 503 | Service Unavailable | Server overloaded |
| 504 | Gateway Timeout | Upstream timeout |

### 14.3 Pagination Patterns

| Pattern | Example | Pros | Cons |
|---------|---------|------|------|
| **Offset** | `?page=3&limit=20` | Simple, jump to any page | Slow for large offsets, inconsistent with inserts |
| **Cursor** | `?cursor=abc123&limit=20` | Consistent, performant | Can't jump to arbitrary page |
| **Keyset** | `?after_id=500&limit=20` | Fast (uses index), consistent | Only sequential traversal |

### 14.4 Idempotency

An operation that produces the same result regardless of how many times it's called.

| Method | Idempotent? | Safe? |
|--------|------------|-------|
| GET | Yes | Yes |
| PUT | Yes | No |
| DELETE | Yes | No |
| POST | **No** | No |
| PATCH | **No** (can be) | No |

**Making POST idempotent:**
- Use idempotency keys: `Idempotency-Key: uuid-1234`
- Server stores result for that key
- Repeated calls return stored result

### 14.5 API Rate Limiting Algorithms

| Algorithm | Description |
|-----------|------------|
| **Token Bucket** | Tokens added at fixed rate; request consumes token; bucket has max capacity |
| **Leaky Bucket** | Requests added to queue; processed at fixed rate; overflow rejected |
| **Fixed Window Counter** | Count requests in fixed time windows; reject if over limit |
| **Sliding Window Log** | Log each request timestamp; count in sliding window |
| **Sliding Window Counter** | Weighted combination of current and previous window counts |

