## 19. Security in System Design

### 19.1 Authentication & Authorization

| Concept | Description |
|---------|------------|
| **Authentication (AuthN)** | Who are you? (identity verification) |
| **Authorization (AuthZ)** | What can you do? (permission check) |

### 19.2 Authentication Methods

| Method | How It Works | Use Case |
|--------|-------------|----------|
| **Session-based** | Server stores session; client sends session ID cookie | Traditional web apps |
| **Token-based (JWT)** | Server issues signed token; client sends in header | APIs, SPAs, mobile |
| **OAuth 2.0** | Delegated authorization via authorization server | Third-party access |
| **API Key** | Static key in header/query param | Server-to-server, simple APIs |
| **mTLS** | Mutual TLS certificate verification | Service-to-service |

### 19.3 JWT Structure

```
Header.Payload.Signature

Header: { "alg": "HS256", "typ": "JWT" }
Payload: { "sub": "user123", "role": "admin", "exp": 1720000000 }
Signature: HMAC-SHA256(base64(header) + "." + base64(payload), secret)
```

### 19.4 OAuth 2.0 Flows

```
Authorization Code Flow (most secure, server-side apps):

[User] → [Client App] → [Auth Server /authorize] → [User Login/Consent]
                                                          ↓
[Client App] ← [Auth Code] ← [Redirect]
     ↓
[Client App] → [Auth Server /token] (auth code + client secret)
     ↓
[Access Token + Refresh Token]
```

### 19.5 Security Best Practices

| Practice | Description |
|----------|------------|
| HTTPS everywhere | Encrypt all traffic |
| Input validation | Prevent injection attacks |
| Rate limiting | Prevent DDoS and brute force |
| Least privilege | Minimum required permissions |
| Defense in depth | Multiple security layers |
| Secrets management | Use Vault, KMS; never hardcode |
| CORS configuration | Restrict allowed origins |
| WAF (Web Application Firewall) | Filter malicious traffic |
| Encryption at rest | Encrypt stored data |
| Encryption in transit | TLS/SSL for data in motion |
| Audit logging | Track all access and changes |

### 19.6 Common Attacks & Mitigations

| Attack | Description | Mitigation |
|--------|------------|------------|
| **SQL Injection** | Injecting SQL via input | Parameterized queries, ORM |
| **XSS** | Injecting scripts into web pages | Input sanitization, CSP headers |
| **CSRF** | Forged requests from authenticated user | CSRF tokens, SameSite cookies |
| **DDoS** | Overwhelming with traffic | Rate limiting, CDN, WAF |
| **Man-in-the-Middle** | Intercepting communication | HTTPS, certificate pinning |
| **Brute Force** | Trying many passwords | Rate limiting, account lockout, MFA |

