### 21.6 Design Uber / Ride-Sharing

**Requirements:**
- Rider requests ride
- Match with nearby driver
- Real-time location tracking
- ETA calculation
- Payment processing
- Trip history

**Architecture:**
```
[Rider App] → [Load Balancer] → [API Gateway]
[Driver App]                         │
                    ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
                    ↓                ↓                ↓
             [Trip Service]   [Location Service]  [Matching Service]
                    │                │                ↓
                    ↓                ↓           [Geospatial Index]
             [Trip DB]        [Location Cache]   (QuadTree / GeoHash)
             (PostgreSQL)     (Redis)
                                     │
                              [Payment Service]  [Notification Service]
                              (Stripe)           (Push/SMS)
```

**Key Design Points:**
- **Location tracking**: Driver sends location every 3-5 seconds via WebSocket
- **Geospatial indexing**: QuadTree or GeoHash for "find nearby drivers"
- **Matching**: Find available drivers within radius; rank by distance/ETA
- **ETA**: Dijkstra/A* on road graph; or use map APIs (Google Maps)
- **Surge pricing**: Monitor supply/demand ratio per area

**QuadTree vs GeoHash:**

| Feature | QuadTree | GeoHash |
|---------|----------|---------|
| Structure | Tree (4 children per node) | String encoding |
| Update | In-memory, fast | DB index, moderate |
| Range query | Traverse tree | Prefix matching |
| Best for | In-memory, dynamic | Database, static |

