### 21.9 Design a Search Autocomplete / Typeahead

**Requirements:**
- Show top suggestions as user types
- Response time < 100ms
- Based on popularity / relevance
- Personalized (optional)

**Architecture:**
```
[Client] → [CDN (cached popular prefixes)]
         → [Load Balancer] → [Autocomplete Service]
                                    │
                             [Trie in Memory]
                                    │
                         [Offline Pipeline]
                         (Hadoop/Spark → Build/Update Trie)
                                    │
                         [Analytics DB]
                         (Query frequency logs)
```

**Key Design Points:**
- **Data Structure**: Trie (prefix tree) stored in memory
- **Ranking**: Top K suggestions per prefix node
- **Update**: Offline batch job every few hours (not real-time)
- **Storage**: Serialize trie; replicate across servers
- **Sampling**: Don't log every query; sample 1 in N
- **Filtering**: Remove offensive / inappropriate terms

**Trie Structure:**
```
Root
├── c
│   ├── a
│   │   ├── r → [car (100K), card (50K), care (30K)]
│   │   └── t → [cat (80K), catch (20K)]
│   └── o
│       └── d → [code (90K), coding (60K)]
└── d
    └── o
        └── g → [dog (70K), dogs (40K)]
```

