### 21.10 Design a Web Crawler

**Requirements:**
- Crawl billions of web pages
- Politeness (respect robots.txt, rate limit per domain)
- Handle duplicates
- fault-tolerant
- Scalable

**Architecture:**
```
[Seed URLs] → [URL Frontier (Priority Queue)]
                     │
              [URL Fetcher Workers (distributed)]
                     │
         ┌───────────┼───────────┐
         ↓           ↓           ↓
  [DNS Resolver] [HTTP Client] [robots.txt cache]
         ↓
  [HTML Parser] → [Content Seen?] → Yes → Skip
         │              ↓ No
         ↓        [Content Store]
  [URL Extractor]
         ↓
  [URL Seen?] → Yes → Skip
       ↓ No
  [URL Frontier]  (repeat)
```

**Key Components:**
- **URL Frontier**: Priority queue + politeness queue (per domain rate limit)
- **Deduplication**: Bloom filter (URL seen), SimHash (content similarity)
- **DNS caching**: Local DNS cache to avoid repeated lookups
- **Distributed**: Multiple workers across machines, coordinated via Kafka/Redis
- **Trap handling**: Detect infinite loops (max depth, max URLs per domain)

